es throughout the series that on top  of being attendants the Angels also have  the duty to monitor their respective  universe in order to determine its  mortal level my argument was that the  angels are like judges who judge the  worth of their universe and then pass  that judgment on to Zeno it has been  shown throughout super that Zeno does  not pay close enough attention to each  individual universe to actually  determine their mortal level I mean in  the future timeline Zeno allowed it to  get to the point that the masu killed  all the deities and nearly took over the  entire multiverse Zeno only acted when  go who summoned him and showed him what  was actually happening so it is pretty  clear that Zeno is not monitoring the  universes himself and the  he is not determining what each  universes mortal level should be this  would explain why the angels tend to  appear neutral and above the fray and  why they tend to act like they don't  feel a personal connection to their  respective universe if my theory is  correct then their job is to be  impartial and to judge and evaluate each  universe just like a teacher's job is to  give an impartial grade to their  students rather than base their grades  on how much they like each student  personally and if we use this same  metaphor then Zeno is like the principal  who decides which students can stay and  which will be expelled based on their  low grades meaning which universe can  stay and which will be erased based on  their low mortal level but that is my  theory let me know if you have other  ones at number 5 what is the grand  priest really up to there have been so  many theories about the grand priest  since he was first introduced many  theories emerged about the grand priest  possibly being evil and the true villain  of the series who is manipulating Zeno  for his own ends others argued that the  grand priest is just a loyal servant of  the Omni King and is merely carrying out  the Omni Kings will on the other 